    11	Bug vs evidence-tier: this is an msolve soundness bug *and* a certificate-philosophy gap. Even a multi-prime `[1]` without a reconstructed `1 = Σ h_i f_i` is not a Q-membership certificate (`CERT-UPGRADE.md` bounds). Here the engine does not even reach a second prime.
    12	
    13	---
    14	
    15	## 1. Source
    16	
    17	### (a) Prime filter: every input coefficient, nothing else
    18	
    19	`src/neogb/modular.h:41-60` (`is_lucky_prime_ui`): a prime is "lucky" (excluded) iff it divides **any** coefficient of **any** generator in the current basis. Not leading-only, not content-only, not intermediate F4 coefficients, not GB denominators.
    20	
    21	```c
    22	for (i = 0; i < bl; ++i) {
    23	  cf  = bs->cf_qq[bs->hm[i][COEFFS]];
    24	  for (j = 0; j < bs->hm[i][LENGTH]; ++j) {
    25	    if (mpz_divisible_ui_p(cf[j], prime) != 0) {
    26	      return 1;
    27	    }
    28	  }
    29	}
    30	```
    31	
    32	First prime, `-g` / `core_groebner_qq` (`src/msolve/lifting-gb.c:1312-1318`):
    33	
    34	```c
    35	prime = next_prime(rand() % (1303905301 - (1<<30) + 1) + (1<<30));
    36	while(fc == 0 && is_lucky_prime_ui(prime, bs)){
    37	  prime = next_prime(rand() % (1303905301 - (1<<30) + 1) + (1<<30));
