+
+### 6.3 Diagnostic subsets and memory wall
+
+Selected subsets were searched only for one-way unit certificates.  None
+returned a basis.  The most informative endpoints were:
+
+- `Mm12` first 100 rows, all pairs: degree 27 after a
+  43,289,616 x 110,262,921 degree-26 matrix, sampled peak 68,628,764 KB;
+- `Mm12` first 120 rows, all pairs: degree 25 after a
+  71,512,101 x 146,166,844 degree-24 matrix, 75,727,692 KB;
+- `Mm12` first 140 rows, all pairs: degree 22 after a
+  34,179,198 x 56,975,773 matrix, 44,514,288 KB;
+- `Mm15` first 128 rows: degree 6, maximum
+  592,068 x 920,701, 22,900,944 KB.
+
+The sole `Mm12` source row containing `c` has source index 121, so the 100-
+and 120-row probes did not even contain the target equation.  Their failure
+cannot say anything about the localized full chart.  Three mechanically
+manifested sparse probes did include the sole `c` row (`Mm12` index 121,
+`Mm15` index 46), all rows at selected high `h` levels, and `z*c-1`; they too
+returned no basis before their limits.  No subset result is promoted to
+survival.
