+setsid nohup ./run_msolve.sh \
+  C_n18m12_M2_9_ell2_s3_V3_8_p1073741827.ms \
+  1200 20 -l 44 -m 1000 > run.driver.log 2>&1 < /dev/null &
+```
+
+`extract_class.py` accepts one class and runs the fixed full-fibre builders
+from their class directories.  It declares an extraction valid only when the
+exact `NATIVE_DONE equations=N` marker exists, `N` equals the physical TSV
+data-line count, and both are positive.  Merely having a TSV header is not
+success.
+
+`run_msolve.sh` records UTC start/end stamps, input and msolve-binary hashes,
+the exact argv, stdout/stderr, `/usr/bin/time -v`, output size/hash, and return
+code.  Runs detached from a GNU `timeout` parent to preserve useful
+computation are explicitly identified in the final table: the wrapper's
+resulting `137` is an orchestration artifact, not an msolve verdict.
+
+---
+
+## 10. Artefact and scope notes
+
+All new computational files are confined to
+`box/moh14-charts-20260905/`; the only ledger-style deliverable edited is this
+report.  No `jc2-lean` or `ideation-*` area was read or changed.  Existing
+unrelated dirty/untracked chart outputs were preserved.
+
+The final local artefact inventory and tool hashes are inserted with the solve
+tables.  Remote jobs were launched with `setsid`/`nohup`; an unfinished remote
+process is never silently described as a timeout or as a completed basis.
+
+---
