+---
+
+## 7. Exact-\(\mathbb Q\) promotion rule
+
+An important msolve limitation changes how a characteristic-zero `[1]` must
+be read.  In the deployed 0.6.5 binary, and also in the tested 0.10.1 binary,
+`-g 2` may stop on a single modular prime when the first-prime Gröbner basis
+is `[1]`; it does not expose a reconstructed rational cofactor certificate.
+The local audit `xmodel/grok-msolve-erratum.md:47-119` documents the execution
+path and a hidden-determinant example.  `qqideal.Ideal.verdict()` inherits
+that behavior.  Consequently this lane types a characteristic-zero msolve
+`[1]` as `UNIT_SIGNAL_MODULAR_ONLY`, not as an exact rational proof.
+
+For every production unit signal the required promotion sequence is:
+
+1. preserve the full input manifest and modular `[1]` output;
+2. re-emit the identical selected generators and `z*c-1` over
+   characteristic zero;
+3. run msolve over the declared rational input as the requested check;
+4. obtain an independent exact-\(\mathbb Q\) certificate, for example a
+   Singular rational `std` result `[1]` on the same full ideal or on a
+   manifest-recorded unit-generating subset.
+
+Without step 4 the fibre remains `TIMEOUT/UNCONFIRMED`, regardless of how
+many modular primes say unit.  Conversely, a completed non-unit modular basis
+does not prove a rational point and is not a Keller pair.  A reported solution
+would still have to be mapped back through the manifest, substituted into all
+source rows and `z*c-1`, used to reconstruct `(P,Q)`, and checked exactly for
+`J(P,Q)=c*x^ell` before it could be called a chart witness.  Lifting that
+chart witness to a Keller pair is an additional theorem-sized requirement.
+
+---
+
+## 8. FALLACY-v2 audit
+
+- **Ring/localization:** every solve uses the manifest-declared field and
+  variable order and includes `z*c-1`; `c` itself is not an ideal generator.
+- **Full versus representative:** only the twelve full fibre builders listed
+  in section 2 can support the class verdict.  Stale envelope unions and
+  subsystem diagnostics are excluded.
+- **Floor versus attainment:** no lower-bound or representative statement is
+  promoted to an attained pair.
+- **Raw remainder / vanished leaders:** this lane consumes the fixed builders'
+  emitted coefficient equations; it does not reinterpret a raw remainder or
+  divide by an unproved leader.
+- **Map:** original-to-safe variable order is explicit and round-trip checked;
+  matching names are never used as evidence of ring identity.
+- **Survival:** neither a bounded-degree no-unit result nor an unfinished
+  modular basis is a nonempty chart.  No point is a JC2 counterexample unless
+  it lifts to a Keller pair.
+- **Other campaign guardrails:** no flag/place/series identification, exit-set
+  price, pole identity, merge-free descent, or arrival-index argument is made
+  here.
+
+This report makes no new exit-price assertion, so no `charge_basis` line is
+licensed.
+
+---
+
+## 9. Reproduction
+
+The orchestration and conversion helpers are:
+
+```text
+box/moh14-charts-20260905/extract_class.py
+box/moh14-charts-20260905/msolve_chart.py
+box/moh14-charts-20260905/run_msolve.sh
+```
+
+A representative full-fibre emission and modular run is:
+
+```bash
+cd /home/ubuntu/jc2/box/moh14-charts-20260905
+python3 msolve_chart.py emit \
+  --class-id C_n18m12_M2_9_ell2_s3 \
+  --stem V3_8 \
+  --characteristic 1073741827 \
+  --output C_n18m12_M2_9_ell2_s3_V3_8_p1073741827.ms \
+  --manifest C_n18m12_M2_9_ell2_s3_V3_8_p1073741827.manifest.json
+setsid nohup ./run_msolve.sh \
+  C_n18m12_M2_9_ell2_s3_V3_8_p1073741827.ms \
+  1200 20 -l 44 -m 1000 > run.driver.log 2>&1 < /dev/null &
+```
+
+`extract_class.py` accepts one class and runs the fixed full-fibre builders
+from their class directories.  It declares an extraction valid only when the
+exact `NATIVE_DONE equations=N` marker exists, `N` equals the physical TSV
+data-line count, and both are positive.  Merely having a TSV header is not
+success.
+
+`run_msolve.sh` records UTC start/end stamps, input and msolve-binary hashes,
+the exact argv, stdout/stderr, `/usr/bin/time -v`, output size/hash, and return
+code.  Runs detached from a GNU `timeout` parent to preserve useful
+computation are explicitly identified in the final table: the wrapper's
+resulting `137` is an orchestration artifact, not an msolve verdict.
+
